the one october memorial committee is  hearing the thoughts of thousands who  took a survey focused on what a future  memorial should include it will  eventually be built at the site of the  route 91 harvest festival 73 percent of  respondents felt education should be a  significant component with support for  the following stories of community  heroism mental health survivor stories  and lessons learned by first responders  in the hospitality industry there was  also discussion about whether or not  people should be allowed to leave  mementos at the site without any  restrictions focus groups suggest they  should be limited or perhaps not allowed  out of maintenance concerns  the families will be worked with closely  to determine  what they're comfortable with what  holidays etc special events for mementos  to be placed  when it comes to the artistic side  respondents backed the idea of having  references to country music and a  symbolic representation of those who  died  and jason aldean is remembering his  security guard ryan fleming in his post  he shared that fleming was the one who  saved him he pulled him off the stage  that night when the shots rang out of  the festival his cause of death though  was not released
 

